What:           /sys/kernel/smart_cache/file
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Write-only SmartCache file policy. Write decimal fd-level
                pairs separated by commas, optionally ending in a newline.
                Levels 1..3 select a registered memory.mctrl.level group;
                level 0 removes the inode tag and migrates its currently
                cache-group-charged pages to the root memory cgroup. The fd
                belongs to the writing task, and is pinned during the write.
                Regular file page cache is supported, including overlayfs
                data files resolved by overlayfs itself. DAX, hugetlb, shmem and
                non-regular files are rejected. At most 64 pairs per write
                and 4096 live inode tags are accepted.

                With enable=1, tagging also migrates existing cached pages
                using real memory/memsw charge transfer, LRU isolation and
                VM-stat transfer. Newly inserted pages are charged directly
                to the selected group. A repeated write retries migration
                and does not double-account pages already in that group.
                With enable=0, tags are recorded, but positive-level writes
                do not migrate pages until repeated after enabling.

                Syntax and all descriptors are validated before mutation.
                Runtime errors can leave earlier pairs and migrated pages
                applied; this is not an atomic multi-file transaction.
                EBUSY/EAGAIN/ENOMEM, EINTR, and the per-file five-second
                ETIMEDOUT report incomplete migration. The requested tag
                remains installed, or removed for level 0, and retrying is
                safe. Concurrent insertion, truncation, copy-up or external
                task charge migration can change the cache after the walk.
                Inode destruction removes the tag; tags do not pin inodes,
                files or mounts after the write returns.

What:           /sys/kernel/smart_cache/enable
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read/write 0 or 1; initially 0. Enables tagged-file charge
                selection and bounded reclaim protection. Disabling takes
                effect for subsequent decisions; an already selected charge
                or in-flight reclaim decision may finish. It does not alter
                page charge accounting or discard stored inode tags.

What:           /sys/kernel/smart_cache/ratio
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read/write percentage 0..100; initially 0. Limits protected
                cache to this fraction of each NUMA node's active+inactive
                file LRU pages, not its RAM size. Level 1 has first claim on
                the budget, then 2, then 3. Each level is also bounded by
                memory.mctrl.max. A group's file LRU remains reclaimable
                while above its effective budget. These sampled VM counters
                are a reclaim policy, not an exact hard allocation limit.
                Urgent reclaim priorities 1/0 and explicit targeted memcg
                reclaim bypass protection, so the policy cannot pin all RAM.

What:           /sys/kernel/smart_cache/stat
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read-only local diagnostics: live tags, successfully migrated
                base pages, and failed page migration attempts. Already-owned
                pages are not counted again. A signal/timeout that aborts a
                walk before trying a page does not count as a page failure.

What:           memory.mctrl.level (memory cgroup v1 and v2)
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read/write 0..3. Nonzero levels are globally exclusive;
                assigning an occupied slot returns EBUSY. Repeating the same
                assignment is valid. Changing or clearing a level releases
                its previous slot. Ancestor/descendant cache groups are
                rejected to prevent hierarchical double counting. Offlining
                clears the slot before CSS can be released. The root file
                is visible for ROM mount-point discovery but positive root
                assignments are rejected. Assignment does not move tasks.
                Existing pages in a removed/replaced group keep their real
                charge until migration/freeing, and lose cache protection.

What:           memory.mctrl.max (memory cgroup v1 and v2)
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        Venus kernel maintainers
Description:
                Read/write page-aligned unsigned byte count, initially zero.
                Bounds this group's protected file LRU pages per NUMA node,
                matching the donor ABI (Venus has one memory node). This is
                distinct from memory.limit_in_bytes/memory.max: it neither
                fabricates usage nor imposes a hard charging limit. Zero
                grants no reclaim protection. Root writes are rejected.
